WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.440
Bangalore feels young and youthful

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.000
and eager to experiment.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.280
Bangalore is actually called
the Silicon Valley of India.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.940
About 42% of Indian startups
are born here every year.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.223
It has has become this
driving magnet for talent.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.830
India's startup scene is booming.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.760
This year alone, the country has seen

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.750
over three dozen unicorns,

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.253
private companies valued over $1 billion.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.480
And much of this impressive
growth has happened

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.170
in record time.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.610
The last decade and a
half, it's a sea change.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:42.570
We live in such a different world today.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:47.570
I think in 2006, if you said
we would have 10 unicorns,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.610
let alone close to touching
maybe 100 unicorns,

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.280
that would have looked madness.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.870
From last September to this September,

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:00.380
there's on an average
three unicorns every month.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:04.000
It's a clear indication
of the ecosystem maturing.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.200
India has had a record year of IPOs.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.350
But with a recent stock launch faltering

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.420
and fierce global competition,

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.900
can Indian startups keep
up this breakneck growth?

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.640
Unlike in the old days,

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.740
when we had to build
everything from scratch,

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.670
today a lot of the infrastructure

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.550
for creating a company exists.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.390
The challenges will be how
to succeed in the business

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.750
before somebody else does better.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.283
The speed and execution is
becoming even more vital.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:42.740
So India's technology story goes back

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.610
at least five or six decades

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:50.440
when the government decided
it needed a strategic location

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:55.440
to start a whole lot of
defense-related technology companies

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.950
that would serve the
government's armed forces.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.570
Since then, Bangalore became the location

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.650
for a lot of those companies.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.410
And to support them,

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.520
a lot of educational institutions

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.160
have come up in and around Bangalore.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.350
The government chose Bangalore

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.840
as the place to build its defense industry

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.930
as the southern Indian city
was considered a safe distance

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.460
from its rival countries
Pakistan and China.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.860
In the early '80s, smaller
private companies also began

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.150
to shift their operations to the city,

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.653
among them Infosys.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:35.140
In 1981, with initial capital of $250,

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.390
seven engineers set up the business,

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:41.320
marking the beginning of the
private tech industry in India.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.290
Today it's one of the biggest
companies in the world,

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:48.053
with a market capitalization
of over $95 billion.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:53.490
Infosys in some sense is
India's original startup.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.800
When Infosys began in 1981,

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.690
it was in an socialistic era

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:04.040
when India was not really that
friendly towards business.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.880
And we had many, many challenges.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.570
For example, just getting
a telephone connection

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.330
would take two years.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.270
To import even a single computer,

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.510
you had to go to Delhi to get a license.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.370
And even if you had to make a small change

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.790
in the configuration of the
computer that you've purchased,

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:22.494
you have to go back and
get the license changed

00:03:22.494 --> 00:03:23.463
all over again.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.530
Then came the economic liberalization

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.420
in the 1990s.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.370
The government deregulated markets,

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:32.860
and reduced taxes and import tariffs.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.850
Infosys and other IT companies thrived.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.230
In 1993, Infosys went public

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:41.890
and built India's first
software campus in Bangalore.

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:45.110
Prompted by this technology
boom in the 1990s,

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:47.960
people from all over India
poured into Bangalore

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.203
to work or study.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.070
Bangalore was the take-off point

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.180
for a lot of those
people that came to study

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.840
and then went overseas to study further

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.950
to get post-graduate degrees or work

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.090
in a lot of these global companies,

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.490
perhaps most of them in the United States.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:07.560
And they made a comfortable
life for themselves overseas

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.030
and never returned.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:13.180
But something changed in
the late 1990s and 2000s.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:15.460
Bangalore became a valid destination

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.680
to chase a career in
technology on its own.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.940
Many local talents,

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.450
especially those from humble
roots, decided to stay.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.503
Lots of overseas Indians
returned to Bangalore as well.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.300
Vani Kola was one of them.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.020
She built and sold two
startups in Silicon Valley

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:37.720
before starting a venture capital
firm in Bangalore in 2006.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.720
I was in India end of
2005 for a long trip,

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:47.340
which I hadn't done in the
two decades that I was gone.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.900
And for me it was just
a very different country

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:51.920
to the one I left.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.850
There was so much confidence,
so much potential,

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.740
so much opportunity.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:05:00.640
I saw a big future for startup India.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:05.640
What I saw was the underserved
consumer experience,

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:07.950
India consumer story,

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:12.820
just ready to embrace many,
many new business models

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:16.060
and entrepreneurship that
could successfully build

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:18.450
very high-scale companies.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.500
But the startup culture itself,

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:25.500
I could trace back to about
2007 when Flipkart was born.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:31.230
So Flipkart is one of India's
two large online retailers.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.930
Two engineers who used to
work for Amazon decided that

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.220
why don't we start an online retailer

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.600
like Amazon by ourselves?

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:42.830
So the two of them got
together in a little apartment,

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:46.350
not far from where I'm standing
in Koramangala in Bangalore,

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.940
and they decided to start Flipkart.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:49.800
Like Amazon,

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.010
Flipkart started out selling just books

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:55.870
and slowly expanded into other
areas, including fashion,

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:59.970
by acquiring e-commerce
startup Myntra in 2014.

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:02.840
Kola was an early investor in Myntra.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:07.570
Flipkart acquiring Myntra
was a really smart move.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:11.660
Flipkart had already
dominated many categories

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.787
except fashion at that time.

00:06:13.787 --> 00:06:16.150
And Myntra was the fashion leader.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:18.720
So it made sense that combined,

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:22.290
they would have the only
real, horizontal platform

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:24.823
that truly came out of India.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:26.793
And today

00:06:26.793 --> 00:06:29.620
Flipkart is one of the
biggest startups in India.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:34.010
The company was bought by
Walmart for $16 billion in 2018,

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:36.450
making the two founders billionaires.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:37.780
The story of Indian e-commerce

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:42.103
started out as definitely not
something that we see today.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.780
I don't think anybody
expected what really happened

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.846
in the last seven, eight years.

00:06:47.846 --> 00:06:49.540
It's been a tremendous journey.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.980
There used to be a time

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:53.860
when a startup and entrepreneurs
in India was shunned.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:57.490
Entrepreneurs or people who
worked in startups told me that

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:59.510
in India's arranged-marriage system,

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:03.100
parents were not willing
have their daughters married

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:06.330
to startup entrepreneurs
or workers in startups.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:08.100
That whole thing has changed

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:12.670
because of people like
Sachin Bansal, Binny Bansal,

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:16.500
the two entrepreneurs who
set up Flipkart and sold it.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:17.950
All of those stories

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:21.750
have now made being a startup entrepreneur

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.820
or working in a startup a
very valid career option

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.423
for a lot of young Indians.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.240
The turning point for a lot
of the technology startups

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:38.030
and particularly the
internet startups in India

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:43.030
has been the arrival of
Reliance's Jio telecom service.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:47.310
Four, five years ago, when
Reliance launched the service,

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:50.750
India had very expensive
broadband internet.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:53.470
Mukesh Ambani, one of
the world's richest men,

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:58.470
decided that he wanted
to offer calling for free

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:03.610
and data broadband internet
services at dirt cheap prices.

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.820
Smartphones were becoming cheaper.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:09.290
A lot of Chinese brands were
introducing really sleek,

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:11.630
inexpensive devices.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.830
So multiple types of internet startups

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:16.250
started getting launched in India.

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:17.770
And particularly in Bangalore,

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:21.210
startup ecosystem started catching fire.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:23.110
A part of that early ecosystem

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:25.920
was online education firm Byju's.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.740
Today it has become India's
most valuable startup

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.190
with 7 million paying users.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.020
Unlike the first generation
of Indian tech companies

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:36.370
who solve problems for global companies,

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:39.130
the current generation
of startups like Byju's

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:41.642
are trying to solve local issues.

00:08:41.642 --> 00:08:45.108
Initial years, when we
were offline scaling,

00:08:45.108 --> 00:08:46.960
that module was a big challenge.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.800
We started this to solve
three big challenges,

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.630
which exist in our education system.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.740
One challenge around
access to good teachers,

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:57.410
learning driven by a fear
of exams, unfortunately,

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.690
and not love for learning.

00:08:58.690 --> 00:08:59.920
And more importantly,

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:04.130
it's impossible to personalize
the way you deliver classes

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:08.410
when there are 30, 35, 40
students sitting in a classroom.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:10.050
To solve those challenges at scale,

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.360
it's very important to use
technology as an enabler.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.500
At the right time,

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:16.930
when smartphones were taking
off, apps were taking off,

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:20.190
we were able to launch
our first learning app.

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:23.070
That's in 2015 August.

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:25.730
And with time, with more
people coming online,

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:28.660
with data becoming better and cheaper,

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:31.760
we've been able to scale our model around

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.007
so using smartphones as
a medium to reach out.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:40.100
2021 has been a breakout year

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.520
for these startups.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:43.460
During the Covid-19 pandemic,

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.920
many consumers have
turned to online services

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:49.780
for grocery deliveries,
tutoring and medical diagnoses,

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:52.170
contributing to surging revenues.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.580
Billions of dollars
have poured into India.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:56.720
In July, for instance,

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:00.540
as in China, the Communist
Party has cracked down

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:02.620
on a lot of these technology companies,

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.860
Indian startups gathered almost $8 billion

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.680
in venture and PE capital,

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:10.980
making India for the very
first time overtake China

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:13.580
as a venture capital destination.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:15.700
Record numbers of unicorns have been born

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.950
at an unprecedented speed.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.380
And investors are hoping
to profit from companies

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:23.170
that could become the
next Google or Facebook.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:27.630
Global investors always
asked, where is the exit?

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:29.840
And in startup lingo that means,

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:33.750
how do I make a return on my investment?

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:38.380
Suddenly, a lot of these
startups have plans to debut

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:39.670
in the public markets.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.900
And now that is a legit exit.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:44.460
And investors then triple,

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:47.150
four times, 10 times their investments.

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.500
That is what's happened this year

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.750
with the public market debut

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.800
of a food-delivery startup called Zomato,

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.810
which was really the game changer.

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:58.660
I think twice in our journey,

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:01.920
we've gotten to a point that
we can't do this anymore,

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.760
and this just cannot be done.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:07.220
But we actually continued
for one more day,

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:11.530
and it all gets sorted
and it all starts again.

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:14.140
Zomato as a company is neither profitable,

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:17.140
and its medium-term
prospects for profitability

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:18.450
are really mediocre.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:22.750
But retail investors have
lapped up the shares of Zomato,

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:25.190
sending the valuation of the company

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:28.820
soaring to $13 billion on debut.

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:30.210
But digital-payment firm

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:34.520
Paytm's IPO in November,
which is India's biggest ever,

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.460
has been a disappointment.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:37.860
It raised $2.5 billion,

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.400
but the stock price has sunk dramatically,

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.550
making it one of the
worst initial showings

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:46.250
by a major tech firm since
the dot-com bubble era

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:48.669
of the late 1990s.

00:11:48.669 --> 00:11:51.710
Like Zomato, Paytm is not profitable.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:53.960
And its IPO debacle casts a shadow

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.280
over other Indian startups.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:57.670
The Indian startup world has to show

00:11:57.670 --> 00:11:59.720
that they are not only building growth,

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:02.100
but also profitability.

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:04.800
When you look at the founders
of the first generation

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:08.720
of companies in India, like
Infosys or Wipro and so on,

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:10.014
they were, as I said,

00:12:10.014 --> 00:12:12.130
they had to be financially very prudent.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:15.300
They had to generate
profits from the business

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.410
and feed that back into the business.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:19.120
Because they were the
only source of capital

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:21.200
that we could reinvest.

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:25.210
Today's entrepreneurs are
encouraged by their backers

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:28.860
to grow quickly, even if they
don't have to make a profit.

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.610
The thesis is that once you grow

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:33.050
and reach a certain critical size

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:35.360
in the market segment of your choice,

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:38.570
then you can always make
your company profitable.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.890
Profitability is still a ways off

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:41.900
for a lot of the startups.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.840
Of course, there is a 1.3 billion market

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:48.420
that on the face of it seems
like a humongous market,

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:50.130
but then there's the other side to it,

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:53.520
that is not enough people
with spending power.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:57.470
It all depends on how many
consumers can afford to buy,

00:12:57.470 --> 00:13:00.830
how much of a middle class
India can grow each year

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.023
and who can afford to buy these services.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.180
India's 40,000 startups

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:12.110
also face other challenges to grow bigger.

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:14.190
Compared with China or the U.S.,

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:17.970
India's internet industry is
still much smaller in size.

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:20.710
And the bureaucracy faced
by India's first generation

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:24.000
of private companies still
exists in some ways today,

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.700
pushing some startups out of the country.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.860
Sometimes I hear frustration echo

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:31.710
through entrepreneurs' voices

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:36.190
when they talk about things
that are needed to, say,

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:41.190
apply for an IPO or get
permission to set up an entity,

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:43.680
how complicated the rules are.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:45.130
Corporate taxes are very high

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.500
compared to countries like Singapore.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.240
And a lot of the
entrepreneurs have then chosen

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:53.060
to shift their basis to
countries like Singapore

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:56.030
because they find that the
tax regime in Singapore

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.863
or elsewhere is much friendlier.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:03.190
While it is easy enough to
start a company in India,

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.700
as you scale,

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:07.700
I think you run into a lot of areas

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:10.300
where regulation is not clear.

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:13.110
One thing would be industry by industry

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:17.340
for government and government
bodies to continue to work

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:20.530
to be a step ahead in terms of providing

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:23.000
clear regulatory guidelines

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:27.793
and continuing to engage
industry in modifying that.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:35.330
But starting up in India
still has advantages.

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:39.650
Half of the Indian population
is under the age of 25.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.210
Young Indians adapt to technology easily

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.800
and could be potential
consumers with spending power

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.020
in the long term.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:49.380
They also provide the country
with a rich talent pool.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:54.240
India has about 4.5
million software engineers.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:57.030
And within the next 10 years,
this is going to double.

00:14:57.030 --> 00:15:00.510
So as the technology talent
improves in the country,

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:03.870
it'll provide a fertile ground
to create more startups.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:06.300
It's still a nascent ecosystem

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.850
just about at take-off point.

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:11.543
But a lot of entrepreneurs
are actually dreaming big.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.650
Entrepreneurship is not
a skill, it's a mindset.

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:18.410
It's a mindset where you
don't take no for an answer.

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:21.010
If you are passionate
about what you are doing

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:23.030
and if that is making an impact,

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:26.070
I'm sure that we can do this for decades.

